{"name":"Beekeeper","hex":"#f6e491","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"beekeeper","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who maintains hives and keeps bees, usually honey bees for the production of honey."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beekeeper"}],"entries":[{"title":"Beekeeper","blocks":[{"text":"A beekeeper is a person who keeps honey bees, a profession known as beekeeping. The term beekeeper refers to a person who keeps honey bees in beehives, boxes, or other receptacles. The beekeeper does not control the creatures. The beekeeper owns the hives or boxes and associated equipment. The bees are free to forage or leave (swarm) as they desire. Bees usually return to the beekeeper's hive as it presents a clean, dark, sheltered home."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Beekeeper_keeping_bees.jpg/330px-Beekeeper_keeping_bees.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beekeeper","wikidata":"Q852389"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Beekeeper.jpg/500px-Beekeeper.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Beekeeper.jpg/1280px-Beekeeper.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Beekeeper.jpg/500px-Beekeeper.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A commercial beekeeper working in an apiary","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeekeeper.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Beekeepers_from_Macedonia%2C_old.jpg/330px-Beekeepers_from_Macedonia%2C_old.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Beekeepers_f